A||||6||FieroLisa||Idiot Mechanics...||||1||
Z||000000||FieroLisa||11-22-2000||09:39 PM||||Is it me, or do mechanics treat women like crap? <BR>I took my daily driver '94 Mercury Tracer to AATCO in Columbus 2 weeks ago. They promised to have the car done in 3-5 days so I gave them a credit card number.<BR>I go away for the weekend and when I get back, I call and they say "Bad news, this will run you $1300 for this and this and this" I said, fine, just get it done, I NEED it by Thanksgiving weekend.<BR>It was supposed to be done last Friday. I call, they say Monday, Tuesday I call and they say they are finishing it up as we speak. Today being Wednesday I decided to run up there and pick up my car. <BR>So I drive there, one of the mechanics came out and said "It's not done, It's a 'no-go'" I about went off on him..."You promised it in 5 days, that was over a 2 weeks ago, I need a car today, what am I supposed to do,and first and foremost why didn't you CALL me to tell me it's not done, etc" He then has the gall to say "Well, m'am, as soon as we diagnose it, we will know. I wanted to see if I could fix it first" So I told him "Well you obviously aren't diagnosing OR fixing much, since my car has been sitting in that parking lot for over 24 hours now. Not only that, the car started before, so this is obviously your fault!"<BR>Oh boy he was speechless. So who knows if the car will be done or not, they said "oh MAYbe by Monday..."<BR>But of course when I called him this evening, 6 hours later, he still hadn't started on it.<BR>AUGH. WHY. I'm so annoyed. <P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fiero5||11-24-2000||06:36 PM||||In any customer service or retail environment, including car sales and car service, you have to make sure people who are wanting your business are not allowed to take advantage of you once they obtain it.<BR>When they give you an estimated time frame and/or amount, unless there is severe circumstances (like the garage had a fire, a mechanic is out sick or was hurt or something) they have to do everything they can to stay within a "reasonable" time and/or amount of the estimate.<BR>There is no excuse for this obvious lack of proffessionalism and courtesy that this place is giving you. If the person you are dealing with is not near the top, like a service manager or something similar, I would highly recommend speaking to one as soon as you can. Make sure you are level headed, courtious and don't lose your temper, at first anyway. More times than not, you will have a better chance of having someone at the top not only listen to you, but actually take action (give you a discount or something) if you talk calm and with facts and specifics. If it sounds like things are still not going the way you think they should, it doesn't hurt to mention all the people you know, where you work or other example that will point out how much damage an upset customer like you could cause if not taken care of correctly. You know the old saying, a happy customer on average will tell 3 people, an upset customer will tell 20.<P>Most places are very customer oriented and are proud of their customer service. If you and other customers never point out incidents like this, those who can make change or just don't stand for this type of crap will never have the ability to fix it and make it right.<P>Speak up intelligently and to the right people, and more times than not you will be happily surprised for doing so. Not to mention saving someone else or yourself from a future incident. If after all that, you are still not happy, then depending on how "hurt" you have been, would make the difference between just not giving them your business and letting as many others you cam know also to taking them to court if you have lost money, time at work, etc.<P>Remember, your the consumer. Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000002||jmw||11-25-2000||09:35 PM||||If it makes you feel any better, it's not just you. I have been ROYALLY screwed, repeatedly. They know they have me by the (excuse me but) balls because I NEED my car. [What are you gonna do, have it towed someplace else in pieces??] I (excuse me again but) freakin' HATE mechanics, yet have a certain respect for them - or anyone who works on cars - because I don't know squat (yet, that is - I'm learning). I just CRINGE at the idea of having to take any of my cars to a mechanic anymore. They have wrecked my trust COMPLETELY. <P>Anyway, the Forum is a good place to check out what things should cost. When I first started restoring my little red '84 I took it for an estimate on painting. Get this - $3100! I'm like "do I have 'stupid' written across my forehead or what?" In my experience, people will charge you whatever they can get away with. BUT knowledge is power so, if at all possible, I try to get recommendations and check out prices on parts, and GET ESTIMATES IN WRITING. [This is not easy to do when you need your car NOW.] <P>I could tell you horror stories all day long, but you get the picture. Just trying to move forward and learn as I go along. I have REALLY gotten a lot of support from the people on the Forum. They have gone out of their way to help me with even the most elementary stuff. What a lifesaver... They're all good guys (even the ones that hit on you -- they don't mean any harm).<P>So, hang in there. Most guys just don't have any idea what it's like for females. It's a completely different world out there.<P>Good luck.||||reg||7
Z||000003||loafer87gt||11-25-2000||10:04 PM||||Get this. This summer my car kept repeatedly stalling and surging on me making it undriveable. It ruined my whole summer as my car spent more time inside the GM repair shop and being towed than it did on the road. Anyways, they replaced pretty well every damn bit of electronics in the car, including 2(!) computers (didn't charge me for one of them, thank god), and it still didn't fix the problem. Finally the guys on the forum told me to check my tach filter, and sure enough it fixed the problem. Anyways, I spent over $1200 Canadian at the GM dealerhip, and over $300 in towing, and it didn't fix a darn thing. I threatened to take them to court, but they said they were just doing their job and the parts needed replacing. Never again will I go to a GM dealership for work on my car.<p>[This message has been edited by loafer87gt (edited 11-25-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||bcibob670||11-25-2000||10:31 PM||||Once again another great reason why I do my own work on my fiero and any other car...<P>I will admit that every new fix up job requires me to buy another special tool...<BR> at least thats wha i tell my wife.<P>actually I enjoy working on cars very much ,but must admit i dont think im good enough at it to make a business of it.  besides I like being a cop and pulling over fieros just to say I like that car!!!! <P>if there is anyone in the mass area who wants some help with their fiero...just email me .  <P>BOB<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000005||KissMySSFiero||11-25-2000||11:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR> He then has the gall to say "Well, m'am, as soon as we diagnose it, we will know. [/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>correct me if im wrong but....did they give you a quote of what it should cost to fix the problem??  shouldnt they find out what the problem is before the try to fix it?  I used to be a mechanic/apprentice at a cadillac dealership.  if we had a car come int with a problem..it was just procedure to find out whats wrong with it before we go and charged the customer $1300 bucks to fix it.  just seemed right.  <BR>on the other hand.  the reason i dont work on cars is because of what i saw.  dont get me wrong.  there are many good honest mechanics out there.  but there are the bad ones that make things go sour for the rest.  i had one of the guys in my class tell me the replace an entire tranny because a 15cent fuse blew.  i personally quit when i broke a bolt on someones car.  i told my service manager i broke it.  he told me not to worry about it and he called the customer and told them it was broke when the car came in and had to be fixed.  it ended up costing the guy 200 extra bucks on tops of the 200 for the water pump.  needless i wasnt there a week more.  <BR>i guess im lucky cuz i can do most of my own work.  but for those who cant or choose not to.  if you find a good mech keep them.  i guess i have vented enough on the subject.  maybe ill post agian to translate all this mumbo.  but good luck and i hope no one gets ripped off out there.  <BR>joejoe||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tina||11-30-2000||12:42 AM||||Rule #1 Never never ever give any garage your<BR>        CC# and tell them FIX IT<BR>Rule #2 Before you fix anything call me to <BR>        authorize repair<BR>Rule #3 Most all mechanics work on commision<P>When it comes to women and cars, it has it's<BR>advantages, never had to pull a part at the <BR>junk-yard.<BR>Plus I always get a lift to the Junker of my <BR>choice in the yards.<BR>When it comes to price, men always get better<BR>price, so have them call first to get Quote.<P>Tina<BR>my other half is one of the extremly rare<BR>honest mechanics. (species almost exstinct)||||reg||1
